{
  "source": "Logic Pro 12.3 User Guide, Apple, 'Drum Kit Designer mappings': the Brush Snare column of the figure 'Drum Kit Designer GM Standard, GM + ModWheel, and Brush Snare keyboard mappings', in Logic's octave naming (C1 = 36) - the GM Standard keys and the brush keys below them - and the page's text: brush circles play while the key is held, MIDI channel 1 picks the hands, 2 the right, 3 the left, and the mute keys stop a held circle on the same hand.",
